{"id":"lm-6761c1b32c1e318ca1d7c664","title":"ALM - Unique European & Slavic Letters","group":"LM Europe","desc":"learnablemeta.com map","cards":[{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/KPYRQsLgrrZA5BTJZjz1ZQXF4cPBnEg0XEnK.avif"],"a":"Cyrillic - Kazakhstan Unique Cyrillic Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Kazakhstan</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/ivCR4rPuODupuGuzRLyQ5dTdkfmVdTSlNh11.avif"],"a":"Cyrillic - North Macedonia Unique Cyrillic Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: North Macedonia</li>\n<li><strong>Info</strong>: Ѓѓ is rare. Ѕѕ seems to be extremely rare.</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/8p5FFbhU0WZoGzSUp1tncLwrwmN2K2Iz8OYo.avif"],"a":"Cyrillic - Russia Unique Cyrillic Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Russia</li>\n<li><strong>Info</strong>: Ээ not to be confused with Зз.</li>\n<li><strong>Warnings</strong>: Technically Ы is found in Russian\\Kazakh\\Kyrgyz\\Mongolian but not in Central European Cyrillic alphabets, but in practice it can be seen in most Cryillic speaking countries.</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/r8G8knH12wEteg19FWTsuf2gzWpPtrAkUfJV.avif"],"a":"Cyrillic - Ukraine Unique Cyrillic Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Ukraine</li>\n<li><strong>Info</strong>: Ґґ is very rare.</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/DSUhQJDliu3QNWNCOycJr4GBVFagK7Dyopz6.avif"],"a":"Greek - Greece Unique Greek Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Greece</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/Fw94zvYD2nrDEs7L3SvzrBU7cC9OzBu585Rs.avif"],"a":"Latin - Czechia Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Czechia</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/HOArMvy52vWgNHxif0qA1IhvUzHIRDK4dnE0.avif"],"a":"Latin - France Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: France</li>\n<li><strong>Info</strong>: While the Œ ligature, unique to French, is found in other French speaking countries, in practice it will usually be expanded to OE, so if you see it on signage within Europe, you are far more likely to be in France.</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/gjyKUVVobJcHj8aTvEgS3YizJAgqHSf5wa7e.avif"],"a":"Latin - Hungary Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Hungary</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/g5RJ7X2gP7zUGHagxAeRBNQSpsAnkWE9MqXo.avif"],"a":"Latin - Iceland Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Iceland</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/GlXujnl4S6XbbUB5G8AGe5XkqRJYTA9J82aO.avif"],"a":"Latin - Italy Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Italy</li>\n<li><strong>Info</strong>: While Ìì (I with grave) is also found in Scottish\\Welsh Gaelic, in practice you are very unlikely to see it.</li>\n<li><strong>Warnings</strong>: Careful with this one, easy to confuse with Íí (which is found in other European languages) and normal stylized Ii's in certain fonts.</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/dOVDbGkEo10uwWysiJtf3p1Un9V00NnkmYGe.avif"],"a":"Latin - Latvia Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Latvia</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/jYF90FvVv9V9HX2ZcAfaMd7OVK0wVHmtDMmm.avif"],"a":"Latin - Lithuania Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Lithuania</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/NxvimhU3VdD0K7KhUtz4zKwuaf8VyuVqtchP.avif"],"a":"Latin - Malta Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Malta</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/4J7KjXoY75Th2unvRXpGzkPnaM68uEfuNjQH.avif"],"a":"Latin - Poland Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Poland</li>\n<li><strong>Info</strong>: While Śś and Źź are also technically found in Montenegrin (Latin), they are very unlikely to show up in streetview there.</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/hzKECiz7PHHhIvrQNwrqxF63v7tQQYEukSq1.avif"],"a":"Latin - Portugal Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Portugal</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/5wJCGkOkDPk3GbbAVJtFKLR2lz647lUkImZ2.avif"],"a":"Latin - Romania Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Romania</li>\n<li><strong>Warnings</strong>: Be careful not to confuse Șș with the Turkish Şş. Ââ can also be found in Sami regions.</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/N4cNPe36dE51phKLluR2ye1gRoELWA52iCTU.avif"],"a":"Latin - Slovakia Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Slovakia</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/2WGUNT1OSpI1mXS5Pfx4JdxRgyZIDsppOO3F.avif"],"a":"Latin - Spain Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Spain</li>\n<li><strong>Info</strong>: Ññ (sometimes written as N with a ¯ [Macron diactiric] above instead), found in Spanish, is effectively unique to Spain (within Europe), though possible rarely in France and perhaps elsewhere via minor languages such as Basque.</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/FeFX3hWiJHm23Iwr81MrqMbfYS3L6KY8W1sz.avif"],"a":"Latin - Turkiye Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Turkiye</li>\n<li><strong>Info</strong>: İi, while a distinct letter, can obviously be confused with other forms of i. It's quite recognisable on signs as Turkish though, so it's been included.</li>\n<li><strong>Warnings</strong>: Be careful not to confuse Şş with the Romanian Șș. Ğğ can also be found in Sami regions.</li>\n</ul>"},{"q":["https://learnablemeta.com/images/33/ofR7hClGZdWZklJRaDNqXQg9OUuVX9CZpUAh.avif"],"a":"Latin - Wales Unique Latin Letters","slug":null,"note":"<ul>\n<li><strong>Countries</strong>: Wales</li>\n<li><strong>Unique Letters</strong>: <code>Ŵŵ</code> <code>Ŷŷ</code></li>\n<li><strong>Info</strong>: Both quite rare, but Ŵŵ more so. Welsh itself is fairly uncommon in streetview.</li>\n</ul>"}]}